    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1001">

                <pb facs="1159" n="963" xml:id="pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/7–3045:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1001<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary
                            of State to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-31">July 31 [1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>164. Following telegram (re <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 419, July 30<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1001-f1"/>) was sent to Stockholm on July 26:<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1001-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Dept learns (your military attaché’s
                            677 [<hi rendition="#italic">667</hi>] to War
                            Dept July 24<anchor n="3"
                                xml:id="d1001-f3"/>) Sov Govt will ask Swedish Govt to deliver
                            interned German airplanes to Sov Govt as war booty. Should report be correct it is desirable that
                            you, preferably supported by your British and French colleagues,<anchor
                                n="4" xml:id="d1001-f4"/> should inform Swedish Govt that we cannot
                            acknowledge such a war booty theory and
                            that Swedish Govt should not therefore permit disposition of German
                            property or equipment as war booty. In
                            our opinion, all German assets and interests are now under the joint
                            jurisdiction of the four occupying powers and should not be removed or
                            disposed of without consent of Allied Control
                    Commission.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
